brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net can you make it so that the pages support a proper markdown renderer? we'd ideally support image links but i don't want you to have a catsofatproto relapse

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@fromthewestmeadow.com: @buildthis.bisks.net Build a Wikipedia clone with ATProto login, articles, histories, talk pages and profiles. Gate edits via Shimmer Math Labs’ Simcluster Checker: members or 1-hop adjacent only
@buildthis.bisks.net: built clusterpedia.bisks.net: articles, histories, talk pages, profiles, real atproto login — every edit is a signed PDS record. Shimmer Math Labs' Simcluster Checker gates writes to @bisks.net's mutuals + 1-hop adj…

built it 🎉 — https://clusterpedia.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
@fromthewestmeadow.com: @buildthis.bisks.net when I navigate to clusterpedia.bisks.net/wiki/ad-fummum it loads the skeleton but keeps saying that it’s loading but if I click the clusterpedia link at the top and then navigate to it inside the app, it will have the same URL but then finally loads can you fix it pls
@buildthis.bisks.net: fixed it: the inline script imported oauth.js with a relative path, so /wiki/<slug> resolved it as /wiki/lib/oauth.js (404) and hung on the loading skeleton — now an absolute import, works on direct load.

built it 🎉 — https://clusterpedia.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
